    "ItemStyle": "single-select",
    "Stem": "Meridian Corporation's accounting department has one employee who opens the mail, records cash receipts in the ledger, prepares the daily bank deposit, and reconciles the bank statement each month. Which of the following best describes the internal control weakness in this arrangement?",
    "CorrectChoice": "B",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "Segregation of duties requires that incompatible functions be separated among different individuals to reduce the risk of error or fraud. The four functions described — custody of incoming cash (opening mail), recording cash receipts (ledger entries), preparing deposits (asset custody), and reconciliation (independent verification) — should be divided among at least two, and ideally three or four, different employees. When one person performs all four, they can misappropriate cash and conceal the theft by manipulating the records and the reconciliation. The specific weakness is that this employee has both custody of assets and record-keeping authority, which are incompatible duties under COSO's control activities principle. A properly designed system would separate cash handling from recording and reconciliation, ensuring that no single individual controls a transaction from initiation to final recording.",
    "SourceDescription": "Original CMA Part 1 exam-style practice item. Not real CMA exam content and not copied from official samples. Replaces archived P1-EC-001 through P1-EC-005 clone rotation group.",
    "QuestionID": "P1-E-R01",
    "question_state": "Certified",
    "Part1OnlyFlag": true,
    "ReviewNote": "If missed or marked, review segregation of duties under COSO Control Activities and the concept of incompatible functions.",
    "CalculationItem": false,
    "Choices": {
      "A": "The employee lacks sufficient training in internal control principles to perform all four functions accurately",
      "B": "The employee has both custody of cash and record-keeping authority, which are incompatible duties that should be segregated",
      "C": "The accounting department is understaffed, which creates an inherent risk that cannot be mitigated through controls",
      "D": "The employee has authorization authority over cash transactions without proper management oversight"
    },
