    "CorrectChoice": "C",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "COSO Principle 2 (Control Environment) states that the board of directors demonstrates independence from management and exercises oversight responsibility for the development and performance of internal control. The board's role is oversight, not operations — it governs and monitors, but does not design, implement, or operate the internal control system. Specific oversight responsibilities include: (1) setting expectations regarding the tone at the top and integrity/ethical values, (2) reviewing and approving the overall internal control structure and key policies, (3) evaluating whether management has designed and implemented effective controls, (4) understanding the major risks facing the organization, and (5) ensuring that monitoring mechanisms — including internal audit and external auditor communications — provide timely, relevant information about control effectiveness. Under SOX, these responsibilities are particularly acute for the audit committee, which must establish procedures for handling complaints about accounting and internal control matters (SOX 301.4). The board oversees; management executes. Confusing the two is a common CMA exam trap.",
